# Testing Conventions

## Harness

- Integration tests: `packages/excalidraw/tests/` using `render` from `test-utils.ts`
- Helpers: `tests/helpers/api.ts` (`API.createElement`), `helpers/ui.ts`, `queries/toolQueries.ts` (`getByToolName`, `toolbar-${TOOL_TYPE}`)
- Element unit tests: `packages/element/tests/`
- Use `reseed(7)` in drag-create tests for determinism

## Running tests

```bash
# Focused (preferred)
yarn test:app --watch=false packages/excalidraw/tests/<file>.tsx

# Update snapshots (deliberate — review diffs)
yarn test:update
# or: yarn test:app --update --watch=false <path>
```

## Snapshot rules

- Snapshots live in `__snapshots__/` beside test files
- After UI/export/restore changes, update snapshots intentionally and review churn
- Do not blind-accept large snapshot diffs — use `snapshot-reviewer` subagent to classify
- Toolbar order, seed values, and i18n key changes often cause expected churn

## Gotchas

- `actionStyles.test.tsx`: assertion failures may be real bugs; worker IPC crashes are a known flake — distinguish the two
- Prefer `API.createElement` over hand-built element objects
- End verification with `yarn test:typecheck` after type union changes
